{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U8 (IIS2MDCTR)", "NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["U8.4", "U8.5", "NAVC1.55", "NAVC1.56"],
      "nets": ["I2C4_SCL_NAVC", "I2C4_SDA_NAVC"],
      "observed": "On the 'NAVC Peripherals' sheet the magnetometer U8 (IIS2MDCTR) has its SCL/SPC (pin 4) and SDA/SDI/SDO (pin 5) tied to the nets I2C4_SCL_NAVC / I2C4_SDA_NAVC. These two nets appear nowhere else in the drawing: they are not connected to the MCU (the corresponding I2C4 pins PF6/PF7 on NAVC1 carry no-connect 'x' markers), and they have no pull-up resistors (the NAVC I2C pull-up block R28-R31 only pulls up I2C1_* and I2C2_*). Every other NAVC I2C device (U5 BMI088, U6 TMP100, U7 MPRLS, U9 EEPROM) is instead wired to I2C1_SCL_NAVC / I2C1_SDA_NAVC, which is pulled up and connected to the MCU.",
      "expected": "The magnetometer should share an MCU-driven, pulled-up I2C bus (the I2C1_* bus used by all the other NAVC sensors) so it can be addressed at 0x1E, as the specification's component table requires ('Magnetometer | ST IIS2MDCTR, I2C addr 0x1E').",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NAVC Peripherals sheet: U8 IIS2MDCTR pin 4 SCL/SPC -> label 'I2C4_SCL_NAVC', pin 5 SDA/SDI/SDO -> label 'I2C4_SDA_NAVC'; U5/U6/U7/U9 all -> 'I2C1_SCL_NAVC'/'I2C1_SDA_NAVC'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Navigation Computer sheet: NAVC1 PF6/PF7 pins marked with no-connect 'x'; I2C pull-up resistors R28-R31 labelled I2C1_*/I2C2_* only"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Magnetometer | NAVCPeripherals | ST IIS2MDCTR, I2C addr 0x1E"}
      ],
      "impact": "The magnetometer's I2C lines are left floating (no master, no pull-ups), so the IIS2MDCTR cannot be read. The board loses all magnetometer/heading data, degrading the Kalman-filter state estimation the design depends on, even though the part is populated and powered.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power, FCC/NAVC MCU, PWM, flash, EEPROM and current-sense sections match the specification (the barometer RESET/EOC swap is the documented V1 bug, not an anomaly). The one drawing-supported deviation is that the magnetometer U8 is wired to I2C4_* nets that are not connected to the MCU and not pulled up, while every other NAVC sensor sits on the working I2C1 bus, leaving the magnetometer non-functional."
}

